<title>UK: INSIGHT - Gold stuck in mid-range, PGMs look sound.</title>
<headline>INSIGHT - Gold stuck in mid-range, PGMs look sound.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> SPOT     NY CLOSE  * SUPPORT * RESIST * RSI14 *   MA10 *   MA30</p>
<p> GOLD   347.55/7.85 *  345.00 * 350.00 *    57 * 343.97 * 343.80</p>
<p> SILVER   4.83/4.85 *    4.75 *   4.92 *    52 *   4.79 *   4.75</p>
<p> PLAT   395.05/6.05 *  385.00 * 400.00 *    71 * 381.13 * 374.20</p>
<p>-----------------VIEWS FROM THE MARKET - May 15 --------------</p>
<p>Gold bullion prices are expected to be restrained by continued uncertainty over central bank sales, with the market stuck between $345 and $350.</p>
<p>Analysts said, however, that ongoing strength in platinum group metals (PGMs) will bolster both gold and silver.</p>
